## Resolved — parameter counts verified 2026-08-06, re-verified 2026-08-07

Recomputed directly from the step-5000 `state_dict` of one delay-0 seed-1 run per size —
now by a checked-in script, `scripts/param_counts.py`, writing `logs/param_counts.md`, so
the numbers are reproducible rather than asserted. It sums every tensor in the saved
state dict and splits out `wte.weight` + `lm_head.weight`, and it asserts that the
`model_config` stored beside the weights agrees with the weights (layers, width, vocab).
It does.

**The design-document labels are exact**: 11,536,640 / 23,204,736 / 60,304,000, i.e.
11.54M / 23.20M / 60.30M against the claimed ~11.5 / 23.2 / 60.3, with non-embedding
3,148,032 / 10,621,824 / 39,332,480 and embedding-and-head shares 72.7 % / 54.2 % / 34.8 %.
Spans are 5.23× total and 12.49× non-embedding, which round to the 5.2× and 12.5× in §2.1.
No number in the paper changes, and the abstract's "11M–60M" range stands.

**One §2.1 sentence did change.** The same checkpoints carry `train_config`, and it
contradicted the draft's "checkpointing every 100 steps": that interval holds for the 23M
arithmetic runs, but 11M and 60M ran at 1,250 and the size sweep at 2,500. Corrected in
place, with the reason it does not matter (triggers fire on step count, not on checkpoint
boundaries) stated rather than left implicit. Head counts, which tensor shapes cannot
recover, are confirmed 8 / 8 / 10 from the stored config. Also noted for the record: one
run in `checkpoints/` — a 10,000-step syntax training-length check — is not 5,000 steps and
is not reported in the paper, so §2.1 now says "every run reported here".

What the check *did* surface is the embedding share, now stated in §2.1: the smallest model
is 72.7 % embedding-and-head, the largest 34.8 %, so non-embedding capacity spans 12.5×
where total parameters span 5.2×. This is a consequence of the untied-embeddings decision
(taken for intervention cleanliness, §2.1) interacting with a fixed 16,384 vocabulary across
all three sizes. It does not alter any computed slope — those use total parameters, as
pre-registered — but it is a real caveat on reading our size axis, and it independently
supports the §2.5 floor exclusion: at 11M only 3.15M parameters are doing computation.
